  "note": "Annual election of one third: five seats, four vacant by rotation and the fifth by the resignation of H. C. Malcolm. J. W. Pollock, town clerk and returning officer, received only four nominations on Friday 5 May; at 5 p.m., no further nominations having been received, he declared the four elected. The fifth seat was left unfilled at this election. Labels: the council was wholly Unionist. This was the last Lurgan election before the wartime postponement; the next was in September 1946."
